    "dex.anemonet": "Its tendrils tune to whatever brushes them — then play it back wrong, with interest. Tide-pool guides carry two antidotes and one apology.",
    "dex.brinargo": "It races the ebb in broad, lazy strokes that fool every predator into mistiming the lunge. Largo, the fishers call it — then it's gone.",
    "dex.conchord": "Its spiral shell is a natural horn, and storms play it from three bays away. Coast families read tomorrow's weather in tonight's key.",
    "dex.dunelay": "It surfs collapsing dunes on splayed stone toes, riding each slide to the exact note of rest. The coast road moves every year; the Dunelay's beach never does.",
    "dex.fogato": "It condenses where the song thins, which on the Quiet Coast is most mornings. Lighthouse keepers log fogato sightings instead of fog.",
    "dex.gullegro": "It steals sandwiches on the downbeat, always the downbeat. Port Calando's dockers eat in 3/4 time out of spite.",
    "dex.kelpitan": "It anchors whole kelp forests to its shoulders and hums them taut against the current. Divers moor to a Kelpitan with its permission, paid in crabs.",
    "dex.largotide": "Grown vast and patient, it surfaces exactly once per tide to take one enormous breath. Harbor records note ships rescheduling around it.",
    "dex.maridian": "Its tideline shell rings the harbor hours more reliably than the harbor bell. Port Calando sets its clocks to a creature that has never been on time for anything else.",
    "dex.sirenetta": "Sailors swear its evening phrase names the one who hears it. The Conservatory lists that as folklore; the coast lists the Conservatory as inland.",
    "motif.anemonet": "Anemonet",
