    "dex.ampurr": "Its purr browns out streetlamps one block at a time, in order. Innkeepers along its route bill the Conservatory for candles.",
    "dex.brasshorn": "Herds winter-call in staggered fifths that carry across two valleys. Drovers say a lone Brasshorn is just a herd that hasn't answered yet.",
    "dex.clockerel": "It crows at intervals so exact the port replaced its bell tower with a perch and an apology. Sailors call its third crow the honest one.",
    "dex.crescendola": "Each generation, a handful are born hearing the whole score at once. Most go quiet young; the coast keeps a list of the ones who didn't.",
    "dex.forgeling": "It sleeps in cooling slag and wakes with the shift bell, already in rhythm. Calando smiths apprentice under one before they touch a hammer.",
    "dex.graviole": "It is, as far as anyone can measure, a boulder that learned the root of the world's chord. Anchor surveyors leave offerings — calibration weights, mostly.",
    "dex.lullaby": "It sings the old cradle-song of whatever hears it, in the singer's mother's voice. TACET grunts carry one each; nobody asks where they sleep.",
    "dex.mutewing": "Its wings cancel their own sound a half-beat after making it — the silence arrives late, like an echo of nothing. Quiet Coast nets catch only its absence.",
    "dex.voltacelle": "Grown into the city's grid, it holds a charge like a held chord and releases both at once. Calando schedules brownouts as concerts.",
    "dex.voltern": "It nests in harbor cranes and rides their booms like perches, discharging on every swing. Calando's stevedores ground their gloves and their grudges.",
    "motif.ampurr": "Ampurr",
